== Independent reference checks <sec:reference-checks>

The arithmetic Asian option has no closed form, but a call on the _geometric_ average of $n$ equally spaced observations does, because the logarithm of the geometric average is normal [6]. It shares the simulation grid and the averaging step with the arithmetic contract, so it tests both. For the up-and-out call, a closed-form price exists under continuous monitoring [2, 4]. Broadie, Glasserman and Kou [5] showed that monitoring on $n$ dates is well approximated by the continuous formula with the barrier shifted to $B e^(beta sigma sqrt(T \/ n))$, where $beta approx 0.5826$; being asymptotic, the correction is expected to agree up to a small remainder.

@tab:references compares both references with estimates pooled over #R.reference_checks.runs independent simulations of #R.exotics.N paths each (#R.reference_checks.N in total). Both agree within their standard errors, with $z = $ #R.reference_checks.geometric.z and $z = $ #R.reference_checks.up_out.z. The continuous-monitoring price without correction, #R.reference_checks.up_out.continuous, would be clearly rejected, in line with @fig:monitoring. As a further consistency check, the arithmetic Asian price, #R.reference_checks.arithmetic.mc ± #R.reference_checks.arithmetic.se, exceeds the geometric one, as the inequality between arithmetic and geometric means requires.

