== Path-dependent options <sec:greeks-exotic>

@tab:greeks-exotic reports the Greeks of the Asian and up-and-out calls under daily monitoring. The Asian call has lower delta and vega than the European call, but higher gamma. Averaging lowers the effective volatility, which reduces vega, and concentrates the distribution of the payoff variable around the strike, which raises gamma, as it would for a European option with lower volatility. The up-and-out call has negative vega: higher volatility makes a knock-out more likely, and this outweighs the usual gain in option value. Its delta is close to zero, because a rise in the underlying moves the option into the money and towards the barrier at the same time. The reference values in the last row differentiate the corrected closed-form price of @sec:reference-checks numerically.

